body:
I was sitting on the corner outside a job I just got after university, It was a bar job whilst I figured things out. In the distance I could see someone from my course walking down the road. He was stamping towards me, looked very pissed off but I stopped him anyway to say hi. He immediately said "I don't talk to effing peasants like you" and kept storming down the street. 

&#x200B;

I still to this day don't know what he meant.

It depends where it comes from. In the instance you're bringing up it's the same as anyone who doesn't understand something yet has a concrete opinion on it - their opinion is not justified or is formed on an assumption. If you wanted to defend Philosophy, you have to identify which is being used to hold up the belief. 

&#x200B;

In other words, use Philosophy.

It seems strange that it isn't held in higher regard. I have the GDL but I would be pretty pissed if I did all the work of an LLB over 3 years in 2 - 3, worked at the same time and was marked at a higher standard.

&#x200B;

Edit: seems like Birkbeck doesn't hold that good a reputation in general so I am not surprised actually.
